# Negative-control mutant — the grouped-count read returns the envelope's rows (AC-19, R36)
#
# Scenario it must flip: contract-product.feature >
#   "See my products grouped by category, with a count for each"
#   (the recorded grouped rows come back as the action's result).
# Test that goes red: contract-product.reads.int.test.ts >
#   "AC-19 the recorded grouped rows come back as the action's result —
#   one entry per category, each with its count". The load-bearing assertion:
#   `loadGroupedCounts()` resolves to `recorded.groupedCounts().total`.
# Mutation: read the envelope's `data` again instead of its `total`. With
#   `limit=count` the API returns `data: []` and rides the grouped rows on the
#   envelope's `total`, so reading `data` yields `[]` and the scenario goes red.
#
# Apply with:  git apply <this file>   (run from repo root)
# Revert with: git apply -R <this file>
diff --git a/packages/headless/src/modules/contract-product/contract-product.services.ts b/packages/headless/src/modules/contract-product/contract-product.services.ts
--- a/packages/headless/src/modules/contract-product/contract-product.services.ts
+++ b/packages/headless/src/modules/contract-product/contract-product.services.ts
@@ -261,7 +261,7 @@ async function loadGroupedCounts(
     withAccessToken: true
   });

-  return (response.total as unknown as ICProdGroup[] | null) ?? [];
+  return (response.data as unknown as ICProdGroup[] | null) ?? [];
 }

